data.body:
Operator 2026-10-13: explore ddflow managing research of any kind (architecture, programming, math, electronics, hardware, signal processing, science): research, follow goals and principles, hypotheses, contradictions, tests, validation, choose paths to explore, proofs, repeat until it settles on the best solution, with the agent's help; standalone or as phases of development; default workflows per task type with their own skills, subagents, pipelines and rules; results recorded and reusable. Reuse as much as possible of the existing and planned core.

Design: research note R-research-flows (web research, 8 default workflows, ranked ideas). Almost everything is an existing or planned engine, configured as data:
- stages = the per-kind gate pipeline ([gates].kind_pipelines.research) with command/agent gates, reviewer family;
- hypotheses, predictions, observations, ruled-out results = reasoning-log steps (P-reasoning: B-rs-model, B-rs-cmd);
- evidence, sources, grades, validity, checks, independent verification = claims (P-research: B-rw-claims, B-rw-sources, B-rw-checks, B-rw-verify);
- the pre-registered plan and the report = document types (P-docs-generic) with the sha stamp / review cursor (B-pi-doc-reviewed);
- runs and observations = jobs and scenario records (B-pi-scenario-run, job add); the skeptic = review lens (B-pi-review-lens); roles and skills = subagent defaults and safeguards (B-sub-defaults, P-safeguards); budgets = cost envelopes (P-safeguards.envelope); re-verification = watches (P-schedule.watch); reuse = research inject/query and the record-contract context and RAG export; sharing = org bundles.
NEW code is only: the workflow template format and its pipeline generator, the plan/prediction ordering rule, the run record wrapper, the stop-rule evaluator, the citation and number audit gate, and the shipped workflow data.

Rules in force: everything configurable (D-everything-configurable), small files (D-small-files), CLI + MCP + prompt from one declaration, logged as events, nothing runs a verifier that is not on the operator's allowlist, an unavailable verifier is recorded unavailable, never passed. Paced per D-usage-pacing-2026-10: filed now, started after the usage reset.
